.nf
YASMV manual                                                 job

.ti 0
SYNOPSIS

.in 3
job list
job show [<id>] [-full]
job wait [<id>]
job cancel [<id>]
job events [<id>]

.ti 0
DESCRIPTION

.fi
.in 3
Inspect and control analysis jobs in the current workspace. Omitting the ID
uses the last selected job. Quote IDs that are not native identifiers.

list displays job summaries. show displays a job's request and summary;
-full includes complete result evidence. events displays a page of recorded
progress events. The agent protocol supports explicit event pagination.

wait waits for completion and imports a returned trace into the native trace
register after replay. show does not change the current native trace.
cancel requests cancellation of an active job. Queries with -async return
immediately so that these commands can be used while the job runs.

Ctrl-C cancels a waiting job. Closing the shell cancels outstanding jobs and
reaps workers. Isolated jobs have a default hard deadline of 60 seconds;
agent requests can set hard_timeout explicitly.

.ti 0
EXAMPLES

.nf
.in 3
>> reach FALSE -depth 10000 -async
>> job show
>> job cancel
>> job wait

.ti 0
SEE ALSO

.fi
.in 3
help workspace, help reach, help check-property, help prove-property.
